# Every environment file, not just `.env`. The config layer reads BOTH `.env`
# and `.env.local` (see `Settings.model_config`), so a developer's `.env.local`
# holds the same API keys and the same FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEYS as `.env` — and
# `COPY . .` would bake it into a distributable image. Only `.env` was listed
# until the Epic 07 hardening pass; the file the application actually prefers
# was not.
.env
.env.*

# Locally stored résumé files (src/infrastructure/storage/local_file_storage.py).
# Real candidate PDFs, and `COPY . .` would put them into an image layer, where
# they outlive any erasure request and travel wherever the image does.
var/
